WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.620
Patrick here in Vancouver, and this is Tesla Short's time, daily for June 6th, 2026.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.680
The headlines today touch on sourcing decisions, market share shifts in Europe,

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:16.120
charging access for other brands, and some real-world quirks that owners are running into with

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.440
the current hardware and software. I want to walk through each one on its own terms, so the business

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:28.300
side, the customer side, and the operational side all get their due. Tesla has added a dual motor

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:34.840
all-wheel-drive Model 3 built in Shanghai to the Canadian configurator, with deliveries expected soon

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:41.680
and a price that lands under $50,000. The move lets buyers here get the AWD configuration

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:48.300
without waiting for any changes at Fremont or Texas. It pulls on capacity that already exists in China

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:54.220
and routes finished cars through standard ocean shipping and import steps. What stands out is that

00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:00.460
this undercuts the earlier AWD entry price even after freight and compliance costs are factored in.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.440
One clear takeaway is that the marginal expense of moving completed vehicles across the Pacific

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:12.200
is apparently lower right now than the cost of retooling domestic lines for the same variant

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:18.560
at current volumes. Another is that Tesla's vertical integration edge is showing up as sourcing

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:25.420
flexibility rather than a requirement for local final assembly. Watch whether the same trim logic

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:31.580
shows up in other right-hand drive or import friendly markets over the next quarter. If it does,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.300
the pattern will tell us how widely the company plans to lean on Shanghai output when North American

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:43.660
lines are constrained. That sourcing choice also invites a closer look at how tariffs, logistics,

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:50.340
and homologation actually stack up against incremental factory investment. The sub-$50,000

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:57.060
Canadian price sits below previous AWD starting points, which suggests the math on ocean freight is

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.500
working in Tesla's favor at these volumes. It is worth keeping an eye on whether this approach

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.980
spreads because it quietly challenges the idea that local assembly is always the necessary route to

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:14.720
competitive pricing. Shifting from North American ordering details to Europe, Tesla has now delivered its

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.900
300,000th vehicle in the United Kingdom and has retaken the top spot among EV brands.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:27.560
The milestone comes from steady model Y and model 3 registrations through the spring months

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:33.140
helped by ongoing price and trim adjustments. After a stretch of stronger competition,

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:39.900
the brand is back in the lead, at least for the moment. One takeaway is that consistent volume on

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:45.540
the two high-volume models can still move the needle even when other manufacturers are pushing new

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:51.540
crossovers. Another is that the next test will be whether that position holds once summer fleet

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:57.140
orders are counted. If it slips again, the pricing and availability tweaks may need another round of

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:03.690
refinement. Further south in France, battery electric vehicles took one-third of new car registrations

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:10.650
last month, with the model Y outselling every other single model in the segment. The result follows

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:16.730
stronger fleet and private uptake after earlier incentive changes. It shows Tesla holding share even

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:22.590
as more European brands bring competing crossovers to market. The practical implication is that the

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:28.490
model Y's combination of range, space, and charging access is still resonating with both commercial

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:35.330
and retail buyers. The data point to track next is how June totals look once final incentive figures

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:41.170
are tallied. Any drop-off there would point to how sensitive demand remains to those policy details.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:48.050
Moving from sales momentum to infrastructure, Ford vehicles will soon gain adapter-based access

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:54.870
to the full North American Supercharger map, including both the existing Magic Doc stations and the wider

00:03:54.870 --> 00:04:00.990
non-magic network. The arrangement expands the usable charging footprint for Ford owners without

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:07.150
requiring fresh capital spending from either company. What matters here is that Tesla's network is

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:13.810
shifting from a proprietary asset into shared infrastructure that other brands can tap. One implication

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:19.190
is that peak hour usage data later this year will show how much additional load the system can

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:25.590
absorb before congestion becomes noticeable. Another is that the deal sets a template for how quickly

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.550
additional automakers could be brought onto the same map if similar agreements follow.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:37.610
On the owner experience side, one model Y driver traced repeated phantom braking and cruise control

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.990
dropouts on straight roads to a spider that had made its way inside the forward camera housing.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:50.110
The case illustrates how a single small obstruction can generate repeated false positives in a vision-only

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:56.370
system. The owner saw the behavior at highway speeds and noted sudden disengagement of cruise control

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:02.390
before spotting the spider during a cleaning check. Tesla has not yet issued a formal service bulletin

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:08.230
on spider intrusion, so owners are left to monitor camera lenses themselves during routine cleaning.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.930
The takeaway is that even minor environmental factors can surface limitations in the current

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:19.610
sensor setup, and the practical step is simply to include lens inspection in regular maintenance.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:26.470
In Phoenix, multiple sightings of cyber cab test vehicles show them without side mirrors and with

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:31.990
the charging port moved to the front bumper. The mirror deletion lines up with the sensor suite

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:38.050
described for unsupervised operation, and local observers note the cars appear to be running in a

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:43.830
limited test fleet. The sighting suggests hardware iteration is still active ahead of any wider

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:50.130
deployment. The next visible milestone would be any regulatory filing that confirms unsupervised

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:56.090
miles driven. Until then, these sightings remain the clearest sign of how the exterior layout is

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:02.350
evolving. The official Tesla account posted a reminder that drivers remain responsible for monitoring

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:08.090
the environment, and the message accompanies the ongoing supervised full-self driving releases.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:14.090
It restates the current operational design domain while software continues to add capability.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:19.750
The phrasing aligns with regulatory expectations that a human must stay attentive,

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:24.830
and future updates will be measured against whether that requirement can eventually be relaxed.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:31.350
One implication is that any relaxation will need to be backed by data showing the system can handle

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:37.930
edge cases without constant oversight. A separate owner noted that the cabin overheat protection feature,

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:44.570
which pre-cools the interior before entry, consumes extra energy yet still feels worth the range

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:50.330
trade-off and daily use. The detail shows how comfort functions can outweigh pure efficiency

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:56.550
concerns once a vehicle is part of regular routines. Another driver mentioned that timelines for

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:02.030
a production intent vehicle may stretch further than initially expected, pointing to ongoing

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:08.330
development hurdles without naming the exact program. That remark fits the pattern of schedule

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:13.770
revisions that followers track, and it underscores how iterative the path from prototype to customer

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:20.490
car remains. Finally, a short post used the phrase, the world is healing in response to a positive

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:26.250
development in the broader ecosystem. The comment captures a moment of collective relief amid the

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:32.710
technical and regulatory debates that run through the space. It shows how even small wins can shift

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:38.290
the tone in fast moving threads. Keep an eye on whether the Canadian import approach spreads to

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:43.210
additional markets in the coming quarter. That will give the clearest signal on how widely Tesla

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:50.530
plans to use Shanghai output when domestic lines are busy. That is the Tesla news for today. TSLA

